<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>More details about bias analysis</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A4.T7" title="In D.4 More details about bias analysis ‣ Appendix D More Experiment Result ‣ Mitigating Coordinate Prediction Bias from Positional Encoding Failures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> reports the ten most frequent individual numbers across all <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x,y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x,y]</annotation></semantics></math> coordinate predictions.
Normal PE = standard positional encodings; shuffled PE = visual positional encodings randomly shuffled at inference time.
All counts reflect total occurrences of a number as either the <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> component of predicted coordinates.</p>
</div>
